.TH MIN 1 "2026" "nimo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
min \- make your computer feel better
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B min
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nimo
makes a Mac feel minimal again: a desktop with nothing on it, a dock with only
the apps you actually open, a calm wallpaper, sane preferences, and a disk
without gigabytes of cache on it.
.PP
Every command that changes something shows what it is about to do and waits for
a yes. Every change nimo makes can be reversed with
.BR "min undo" .
nimo never touches a path outside your home folder and never asks for sudo.
.SH THE PROMPT
Run
.B min
with no command and it opens a prompt. Type
.B /clean desktop
,
.B /wallpaper
,
.B /undo
\- the slash is optional, as is the exact wording. Typos are matched on shared
prefix and suggested, never run on your behalf. Flags work there too. Piped or
redirected,
.B min
prints this help instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B min tidy
Desktop, dock, wallpaper and preferences, in that order. Each step asks first.
.TP
.B min desktop
Move everything on the desktop into \fIDesktop/Tidy/\fR, sorted by kind.
Nothing is deleted or renamed. \fB\-\-undo\fR puts it all back.
.TP
.B min dock
List the dock and remove only the entries you tick. The dock is exported first;
\fB\-\-restore\fR brings it back.
.TP
.B min wallpaper
Choose from the wallpapers macOS already ships with. Nothing is downloaded.
\fB\-\-random\fR picks for you, \fB\-\-restore\fR goes back.
.TP
.B min undo
Everything nimo has done, listed. Pick one and it is reversed.
.TP
.B min clean
Scan for junk, show the total, and free it after you confirm.
.TP
.B min preview
The same scan, unable to delete anything.
.TP
.B min top
The biggest folders in your home, with bars.
.TP
.B min doctor
Disk, memory, battery, uptime, clutter and total junk on one screen.
.TP
.B min setup
Apply a small, sane set of macOS preferences. Every key's previous value and
type are written down first, so \fB\-\-restore\fR can put them back exactly,
including unsetting keys that had never been set.
.TP
.B min update
Run \fBgit pull\fR in whichever folder nimo lives in.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen and change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation question.
.TP
.B \-\-undo
Put the desktop back the way it was.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Put the dock, the wallpaper or the preferences back.
.TP
.B \-\-random
Let nimo pick the wallpaper.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " a,b"
Limit to certain items or setup groups.
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
What counts as an old download. Default 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
How many rows to show. Default 15.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine readable output for \fBclean\fR and \fBpreview\fR. Sizes in bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List what a command would offer, without asking anything.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Plain output. \fBNO_COLOR\fR in the environment does the same.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No banner.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.nimo/config
Optional defaults, one \fIkey = value\fR per line: \fBdays\fR, \fBlimit\fR,
\fBjobs\fR, \fBcolor\fR, \fBtidy\fR. It is read, never executed.
.TP
.I ~/.nimo/undo/
One file per desktop tidy, listing every move nimo made.
.TP
.I ~/.nimo/backups/
The dock as it was, and the wallpaper as it was.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Everything went fine, including "there was nothing to do".
.TP
.B 1
Something could not be done.
.TP
.B 2
The command line did not make sense.
.SH TESTS
.B bash test/run.sh
runs 96 checks against a throwaway computer in \fI/tmp\fR.
.B bash test/macos.sh
runs 62 more against a simulated macOS, so the dock, wallpaper and preference
code can be tested without a Mac and without touching yours.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full documentation lives in the repository README.
.SH AUTHOR
Daniel Kopa.
